    "body": "Verification on `origin/main` f4b351682 (scratch test only, not committed). Result: all cases are refused by name. No program is written.\n\nMethod: one wire section through `engine::run` with `assets/posts/wire-iso.cps` and `crates/app/tests/edm/wire-iso-fixture.mch`. The stream has one `PARAM OriginX <v>` or `PARAM OriginY <v>` line before the section.\n\nControl cases:\n- No origin: `G0 X-30. Y0.`, `G1 X-20. Y0.`, no warnings.\n- `PARAM OriginX 5`: `G0 X-35. Y0.`, `G1 X-25. Y0.`, no warnings. The origin shifts the program as expected.\n\nCases (the `.cnc` parser reads each value as a string):\n\n| PARAM | Values | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `OriginX` | `null`, `nan`, `NaN`, `inf`, `-inf`, `\"nan\"`, `\"inf\"` | `Err(Refused(\"stream parameter OriginX must be a finite number\"))` |\n| `OriginY` | `null`, `nan`, `NaN`, `inf`, `-inf`, `\"nan\"`, `\"inf\"` | `Err(Refused(\"stream parameter OriginY must be a finite number\"))` |\n\nNotes:\n- The refusal is not a script `message()` warning. It is an engine error from `read_finite` in `crates/post/src/post/wcs_rotate.rs`. `engine::run_program_with` calls `wcs_rotate::apply` before any script hook. The scan of `OriginX`/`OriginY` runs for each section, also when the section has no `WcsYaw`.\n- App path: `crates/app/src/posting.rs` maps the engine error to `post engine: <error>` and returns it. So the user sees a diagnostic that names the parameter, and no NC file is written. A shifted program with no warning does not occur.\n- The skip in `wire-iso.cps` lines 199-200 cannot be reached with a non-finite origin.\n\nVerified fixed on f4b351682 by 84583da67 (`fix(wcs): carry Z-rotated work offset through generation and post`, #760). PR #3263 (6e1805bfd) is not the fix for this issue.\n\nPin: none in the tree. The pin that the claimant wrote is not pushed (branch `mkinney:issue/3264-wire-iso-finite-origin` does not exist). No test in the tree asserts the `OriginX`/`OriginY` refusal.\n\nClosing needs the pin in the tree: the claimant can open a PR with his pin test, or the coordinator closes this with the commit named.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
